// The guarded-conversion error rendered past the width of the renderer that
// prints it.
//
// `noUnguardedVars` (Theory/Constraint/System/Guarded.hs:507-514) throws a Doc,
// not a string: an `fsep` over the offending variable names (lines 509-512)
// above `ppFormula f0`, and `ppFormula = nest 2 . doubleQuotes .
// prettyLNFormula` (line 477) is a Doc too, as is the `in the formula` trailer
// `ppError` appends (line 479).  Every break in them is decided by whichever
// renderer receives the Doc, and the same error reaches two:
//
//   - the `theory … end` echo, through `prettyLemma`'s `conversion to guarded
//     formula failed:` comment (lib/theory/src/Lemma.hs:131-134), printed by
//     `renderDoc` at `lineWidth = 110` (Main/Console.hs:242-243,398-399) and
//     HughesPJ's default 1.5 ribbons, so ~73 columns of text;
//   - the wf report, through `checkGuarded`
//     (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:988-993) under the ` Formula guardedness`
//     topic (line 1004), which `addComment` stores as `render c`
//     (TheoryObject.hs:717-718) — HughesPJ's default style, 100 columns and ~67
//     of ribbon — and which nests the message two columns deeper than the echo
//     does.
//
// `WideUnguardable` is written to fall between the two budgets: the echo keeps
// each pair equation on one line and breaks the conjunction, the report breaks
// inside the equations as well, and the variable list wraps after a different
// name in each.  `NarrowUnguardable` fits in both and is the control — its four
// lines are identical everywhere, so a diff confined to the wide lemma is the
// width, not the message.
//
// Both probes are LEMMAS.  `prettyRestriction` (TheoryObject.hs:889-901)
// decides its `// safety formula` line with `formulaToGuarded_`
// (Guarded.hs:466-467), which is `either (error . render) id`, so the oracle
// DIES while printing an unguardable restriction and yields no comparable
// bytes.
//
// Mode `diverge`: the port renders the quoted formula and the variable list as
// single lines in both places.  See check.sh's `divergence_shape` for the
// anchors.  `guarded_freshened_names` pins the same message where it fits the
// budget; no corpus theory carries an unguardable lemma at all.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block AND the `theory … end` echo (see
// check.sh) — the corner is exactly that the two lay the same Doc out
// differently.

theory S3UnguardableWideLemma
begin

rule A:
  [ In( x ) ] --[ Observed( x ) ]-> [ ]

lemma WideUnguardable:
  "All firstArgument secondArgument thirdArgument fourthArgument.
     ( <firstArgument, secondArgument> = <thirdArgument, fourthArgument>
     & <secondArgument, thirdArgument> = <fourthArgument, firstArgument> )
   ==> F"

lemma NarrowUnguardable:
  "All x z. (<x, z> = x) ==> F"

end
